dir="auto" translate="no"><p><span>Create a Final Year Information Technology mini project strictly based on Distributed Systems concepts as per Savitribai Phule Pune University Lab Practice V syllabus.</span></p><p><span>Project Title: "Multiplayer Snake and Ladder Game using Distributed Client-Server Architecture"</span></p><p><span>Requirements:</span></p><ol data-spread="false" start="1"><li><p><span>The project must be a real distributed system, not just a simple standalone application.</span></p></li><li><p><span>Implement a multiplayer Snake and Ladder game using a distributed client-server model.</span></p></li><li><p><span>Multiple clients (players) should connect to a central server over a network.</span></p></li><li><p><span>The server must manage:</span></p><ul data-spread="false"><li><p><span>Game state (player positions on board 1â€“100)</span></p></li><li><p><span>Turn management</span></p></li><li><p><span>Dice rolling logic</span></p></li></ul></li><li><p><span>Clients should:</span></p><ul data-spread="false"><li><p><span>Send move requests (dice roll or button click)</span></p></li><li><p><span>Receive real-time updates of the game state</span></p></li></ul></li><li><p><span>Use real-time communication for synchronization between server and clients.</span></p></li></ol><p><span>Technology:</span></p><ul data-spread="false"><li><p><span>Node.js (preferred) or Java</span></p></li><li><p><span>Use Socket.IO or WebSockets for real-time communication</span></p></li><li><p><span>Keep code simple, beginner-friendly, and well-commented</span></p></li></ul><p><span>Distributed System Concepts to Demonstrate:</span></p><ul data-spread="false"><li><p><span>Client-Server Architecture</span></p></li><li><p><span>State Synchronization</span></p></li><li><p><span>Concurrency Handling (multiple players at same time)</span></p></li><li><p><span>Event-driven communication</span></p></li><li><p><span>Real-time data consistency</span></p></li></ul><p><span>Project Deliverables:</span></p><ol data-spread="false" start="1"><li><p><span>Complete source code (server + client)</span></p></li><li><p><span>System architecture explanation</span></p></li><li><p><span>Algorithm / working logic (step-by-step)</span></p></li><li><p><span>Flow of communication between client and server</span></p></li><li><p><span>Sample input-output (game simulation)</span></p></li><li><p><span>Viva questions with answers</span></p></li><li><p><span>Short theory notes on:</span></p><ul data-spread="false"><li><p><span>Distributed systems basics</span></p></li><li><p><span>Client-server model</span></p></li><li><p><span>Real-time communication systems</span></p></li></ul></li></ol><p><span>Constraints:</span></p><ul data-spread="false"><li><p><span>Keep implementation simple and easy to explain in viva</span></p></li><li><p><span>Avoid complex distributed algorithms like leader election or consensus</span></p></li><li><p><span>Focus on clarity and working demonstration of distributed communication</span></p></li></ul><p><span>Bonus (optional):</span></p><ul data-spread="false"><li><p><span>Simple UI for Snake and Ladder board</span></p></li><li><p><span>Highlight current player turn</span></p></li><li><p><span>Show real-time board updates on all clients</span></p></li></ul><p><span>Make the project academically correct, easy to understand, and suitable for scoring high marks in university practical evaluation.</span></p></div></div><div aria-hidden="true" class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 z-2 rounded-[24px] shadow-[inset_0px_0px_0px_1px_rgba(0,0,0,0.07)]"></div></div></div>
