<p data-start="1096" data-end="1143"><strong data-start="1096" data-end="1143">â€œFrontend nahi hai to client-server kaise?â€</strong></p>
<p data-start="1145" data-end="1158">ğŸ‘‰ tum bolna:</p>
<blockquote data-start="1160" data-end="1392">
<p data-start="1162" data-end="1392">â€œFrontend is served from the same Node.js server using Express static middleware. The browser acts as the client, which communicates with the server over HTTP and WebSockets. Hence, client-server architecture is still maintained.â€</p>
</blockquote>
<hr data-start="1394" data-end="1397">
<h1 data-start="1399" data-end="1419">ğŸ”¥ One-line answer</h1>
<blockquote data-start="1421" data-end="1537">
<p data-start="1423" data-end="1537">â€œFrontend separate server pe nahi hai, but browser itself client hai, so client-server architecture still exists.â€</p>
</blockquote>
